Z||000004||JSocha||06-13-2001||09:40 AM||||A kid (couple years younger then I and after I graduated) here in Rugby bought a brand new '86 Trans Am, fully loaded with less then a thousand miles on it.<P>Parked it at the High School parking lot (typical place to park it here in Rugby) one evening, went crusin with some friends for the evening (as he lived out on a farm), came back to the parking lot to get his car and somebody smashed it with baseball bats, slit his tires and tore up the interior with knives.  The car was totalled and made the Pierce County Tribune newspaper.<P>They never found out who did it, but man, that was cheap if not to mention very, very low.<P>Somebody ever did that to my car, there would have been h#llish retribution from me cause I would have hunted the b@st@rds down and beat the living $h*t out of them and broke every bone in their bodies.  <P>I think I would have been in trouble though, cause if I had to chase them down on foot to get ahold of em, I would be stepping in their $h*t all the way!  And I'm sure they could have ran faster scared then I can mad!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||06-13-2001||10:20 AM||||I'd definately call the TV station and have them do a story on it. Pretty interesting the stuff that can go on in a school parking lot that doesn't get investigated by security. If someone can smash glass and crush metal with a brick (how noisy is that?) what keeps someone from smoking crack or loading an AK-47 in the parking lot?  I think the school and the police department should be held accountable for their (lack of) action.  Today, "Just a bug.", tomorrow "Just a firebomb through the front window of your house." Whoever the culprit of this action was is clearly antisocial and potentially sociopathic.||||reg||1
