Z||000009||Dave Gunsul||06-13-2001||02:19 PM||||What a di**less piece of s*$it!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>I would like to be the first to join the possie that smooth mentioned!<BR>The reason that the school isn't being helpful is because they're afraid that you're going to sue them, which is exactly what you should do!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>BTW why do you think you sound gay just because you give a crap about someone else??<BR>If more people cared even a little bit about each other then this kind of thing wouldn't happen in the first place!<BR>I don't know you or your brother, nore do I own a bug, but I am actually pissed off that <BR>this has happened to you!! It especially pisses me off when it happens to someone that tries to be a good person with the way the world is today.<BR>Please tell your brother that I,for one,am very sorry about his loss and if I lived closer i'd help him fix it.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||8
Z||000010||LZeitgeist||06-13-2001||02:22 PM||||Hell yes!!! That's a *PERFECT* idea!!! Call the local television news station!!! Absolutely, that's exactly what I'd do... damn straight!!<P>GREAT idea!!! <P>(And no, there is NO sarcasm in this post - I'm a serious as a heart attack! I'd be on the phone to them right this minute if it was me!!!)||||reg||1
Z||000011||Ken Wittlief||06-13-2001||03:09 PM||||im a little confused, who said, 'so? its a bug.' ? the police officer that took the report?<P>your brother?<P>right now you need to be more concerned for your brothers safety - trashing the car could have been a random act of senseless violence, or it could be that some very violent and unrational kids have it in for your brother - not to be taken lightly.<P> the car could have been some kind of warning of worst things to come.<P>  I grew up in a poor neighborhood on the west side of buffalo, NY. When I was in grade school every once in a while a couple of kids would get into a scuffle, then things would smooth out and they would either become friends or simply stay away from each other. <P>  everyone on our street went to the same grade school. But when we got into high school, and some kids when to one and others wents elsewhere, and girls and hormones started to become a part of our lives, some of the kids on the street started getting weird, kinda territorial.<P>   It was almost as if they wanted to split the two ends of the street up into us and them, and start some kind of gang thing, and find reasons to have fights in the streets.<P>  one summer things got worse. someone liked to throw bricks at peoples houses for no apparent reason, or to chuck beer bottles as hard as they could at night in random directions, a couple of girls moved onto the street and seemed to stir up trouble.<BR> <BR> till finally one day about 6 of the guys from our end of the block, and about 8 guys from the other end, were out in the middle of the street with chains and baseball bats, ready to 'settle things once and for all'.<P>  to this day I still dont know what the h#ll that meant, or what it was really all about. The summer before I had hung around with some of the kids from the other end of the street, camped out in their backyards overnight, we all got along ok<P>   and there really wasnt anything different about the kids from either end of the block - and here they were ready to smash each others heads in, over nothing. <P> the confrontation wasnt that serious in the end, and I think afterwords we all stepped back and said to ourselves, "what the h#ll were we doing out there". about a year later we all went our separate ways.<P>  If you can find out who did this to your brothers car, keep it on a high level, make them pay to replace the car, but give them space to push this into 'kids will be kids' and try not to make it personal.<P>  that kid in CA that went to school recently and killed a buch of students that were bullying him, wasnt that over a stolen skate board?<P>  if you and the school and the cops can pull this up out of the mud, and keep it from getting personal, then the car can be replaced with something else, maybe not another vintage beetle, but something.<P>  if it gets personal, and it escalates, then someone can end up dead very soon.<P>  and it could be your brother. This is potentailly a very dangerous situation. Someone may be targeting your brother for some reason. You need to get to the bottom of it and de-fuse it.<P>and for the next few months your brother should not be in any situation where he is alone and vunerable - until you find out what this is all about.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Urchin||06-13-2001||04:53 PM||||It must be a beetle thing.  A friend of mine in high school had a 70's bug, nad the exact same thing was done to his.   It turned out to be one girl that was responsible.  Not an ex, just a girl that thought he and beetles were "geekey"  She did a real number on it.  <BR>Windows smashed, keyed it, kicked off the mirrors and windows, knifed the seats, etc.  The crappy thing is, everyone saw her do it, but when the police came, no one would say anything, so she got off scott free.  Unbelievable, sorry to hear that.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature2_3.jpg">   <P>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Formula88||06-13-2001||05:29 PM||||A moment of silence..........<BR>........<BR>........<BR>........<BR>Now.  If you know who did it to your own satisfaction, I'd take care of business.  In any event, I'd suggest suing the schoold for neglegence since they saw something going on and did nothing.  Hold off on retaliation until you know about the lawsuit.  Also, you might get enough info to catch and convict the a$$holes.  And then you can get your revenge later, when they think it's safe.<P>My '72 TA was trashed once (nowhere near as bad as your bros. bug).  That was almost 20 years ago, but if I ever find out who did it, I'll still make them regret it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>I feel for you and your bro.||||reg||1
