Z||000015||trigger||06-13-2001||09:41 PM||||I really feel bad for your brother.<BR>My 88 coupe got keyed twice this year.  Early in the year in my transportation class it got keyed on both right fenders.  I guess he was gonna work on the left but the teacher was coming.  Normally I like the teacher, but he said that he didn't have anybody in his class that would do something like that.  That made me feel really low.  Recently I found out who did it.  Now I just have to catch up to him with a few friends and pound the s$*t out of him, or something of that nature.<BR>Secondly, about two days after I found out who did the first one, my car got keyed between the driver door and filler cap, deep.  It went all the way through the paint.  Let's just say the person who keyed it the second time is living on borrowed time.<P>I may sound like a violent person, but normally I'm not.  This kind of thing just pisses me off.  It's pretty sad when you have to mess with somebody's car just because it's nicer than yours.  Somebody always has a car that's nicer or faster or better.  Get over it.<P>I'm done ranting. <P>Oh, call the news, sue the school, and cops.  When you catch the punks that did this throw a good punch for me.<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||1
